<BaseLayout title="About HisaabLab" description="Learn why HisaabLab builds free, transparent financial calculators for Indian households and how its calculations work.">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><Breadcrumbs items={[{label:'Home',href:'/'},{label:'About'}]} /><span class="eyebrow">About HisaabLab</span><h1>Better decisions begin with visible assumptions.</h1><p class="lead">HisaabLab is a free educational calculator library for Indian households. It translates home-loan and property questions into inspectable cash-flow models—without asking for an account.</p></div></section>
  <section class="content-section"><div class="container content-grid"><article class="prose"><h2>What we build</h2><p>Our calculators help you estimate EMIs, compare prepayment choices, examine rent-versus-buy scenarios, plan a down payment and understand the wider cost of owning a home. They use Indian number formatting and keep every important assumption editable.</p><h2>How calculations work</h2><p>The financial engine uses pure TypeScript functions in your browser. Loan schedules carry full numerical precision internally and round only for display. Reducing-balance interest is calculated monthly unless a page explicitly states a different convention.</p><p>Calculator pages explain payment timing, compounding, included costs and known limitations. Worked examples use illustrative figures, not advertised market rates.</p><h2>What we do not claim</h2><p>HisaabLab is not a bank, broker, lender or registered investment adviser. We do not promise approval, returns, savings or property appreciation. We do not have invented partnerships, professional credentials, testimonials or rankings.</p><h2>How we plan to sustain the site</h2><p>The tools are free. The architecture can support clearly labelled display advertising later, but advertising is disabled until an approved publisher account and appropriate privacy and consent setup exist. Calculators will never require an ad click.</p><h2>Our editorial standard</h2><p>Regulatory claims link to primary sources where practical, source review dates are shown, and automated tests check the financial engine before production builds. Read the complete <a href="/editorial-policy/">editorial and calculation policy</a> for sourcing, byline and corrections details.</p></article><aside><div class="related-box"><h2>Design principles</h2><p>Private by default</p><p>Assumptions over predictions</p><p>Complete cash flows</p><p>Useful before persuasive</p></div></aside></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
